itional symbols  so this could be like uh a or b or c  like these take boolean values and then  based on these propositionals of symbols  we can we can basically build formulas  on top of them the prepositional symbols  are also commonly like known as atomic  formulas and then you can make more  complicated formulas based on these  atomic formulas using a set of logical  connectives so these are negation and or  implication or bi-directional  implication  so let me actually write that here  so  here so we're going to start with syntax  so what does syntax have so syntax has  prepositional  formulas  propositional symbols sorry  so these are like a b  c and so on and then we can have  formulas  defined on top of them and let me use f  for formula and how do i define formulas  i use these logical connectives to to  create formulas these connectives that  we just talked about okay  so um like here are a couple of examples  of how we go about it so we can build  these formulas recursively let's call f  and g formulas here and if f and g are  formulas then i can even build more  formulas on top of them so i can have  negation of f as a new formula or f and  g as a new formula or f or g as a new  formula if implication g or f  bi-directional implication g so like f  is equivalent to g you can think of it  like that okay  here are a few examples so if a is is a  boolean symbol a is a formula by itself  negation of a is a formula  negation of b implying c is a formula so  i've just used a bunch of connectives  and created a more  complicated formula here  uh i can have this guy as a formula  right so negation of a is a formula  negation of b is a formula negation of b  implying c is a formula negation of b or  d is a formula and then or of these and  end of these is also going to be a  formula okay  negation of negation of a is a formula  well why is that because a is a formula  negation of a is a formula negation of  that is also formula  and this guy a negation b is not a